Subject: Compiling a simple concordance with a two-word node expression
Message-ID: <3H5elyVuaCU.hYyd9RsqiMEJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/corpling-with-r/c/3H5elyVuaCU/m/hYyd9RsqiMEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I am trying to compile a single simple concordance for 'may' and 'may
not' as node expressions. 'May's do get retrieved but not the 'not's
in 'may not' cases.

Any tips on how to make it work? I have tried a number of possible
regular expressions for 'may not' but unsuccessfully.

Below is the script I used, it is based on section 4.2 of Quantitative
Corpus Linguistics with R, p.127-135:

DATAFILE<-scan(choose.files(),what="char",sep="\n")
DATAFILE2<-unlist(strsplit(DATAFILE,"\\W+"))
DATAFILE2<-gsub("(\\W)","\\1",DATAFILE,perl=T)
DATAFILE3<-unlist(strsplit(DATAFILE2," +"))
tail(DATAFILE3)

(matches.in.datafile<-grep("(^may$|^may.not
$)",DATAFILE3,ignore.case=T))
DATAFILE3[(matches.in.datafile[2]-6):(matches.in.datafile[2]+6)]
beginning.of.range<-max(1,(matches.in.datafile[1]-6))

conc.outputfile<-choose.files()
cat("PRECEDING_CONTEXT\tMATCH\tSUBSEQUENT_CONTEXT
\n",file=conc.outputfile)

 for(i in matches.in.datafile) {
 cat(file=conc.outputfile,append=T,
 DATAFILE3[max(0,i-6):max(0,i-1)],
 "\t",
 DATAFILE3[i],
 "\t",
 DATAFILE3[(i+1):min(i+6,length(DATAFILE3)+1)],
 "\n")
 }

Thanks for your time!

Sandra

